#====================================================================
# DRAFT-coinutils-ohos-tool-requirements-leak
# Do not carry Windows/MSVC tool requirements into target-only OHOS adaptations
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-coinutils-ohos-tool-requirements-leak
trigger_tool:           conan|shadow-ci|tool-requires
phase:                  l0|dependency-resolution
error_signature:        registry_unreachable.*automake|registry_unreachable.*msys2|tool_requires.*automake|tool_requires.*msys2
severity:               2
category:               conan|tool-requirements|dependency-boundary|harmonyos
match_keywords:         CoinUtils, tool_requires, automake, msys2, MSVC, OHOS, shadow CI, registry_unreachable, generated configure
title:                  Target-only OHOS recipes should remove copied MSVC/autotools tool_requires when generated release files are used

root_cause:             CoinUtils was bootstrapped from an existing recipe that had Windows/MSVC support code and tool requirements for automake
                        and msys2. The OHOS target package uses generated upstream configure files and does not run autoreconf or MSYS.
                        Keeping those copied tool_requires makes L0 dependency resolution depend on unrelated tools and can fail before the
                        actual package is evaluated.

affected_scope:         Recipes copied from cross-platform Conan Center packages into an OHOS-only adaptation where Windows/MSVC support is kept
                        for source compatibility but the target CI only needs generated autotools files.

verification_cmd:       rg -n "tool_requires|automake|msys2" archives/c/coinutils/2.11.12/conanfile.py

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           remove-unneeded-tool-requires-from-ohos-package
rec_description:        If the OHOS build path does not execute autoreconf and does not use MSYS, remove copied tool_requires for automake/msys2.
                        Keep any MSVC branches only if they are harmless recipe compatibility code, and make the OHOS path depend on the
                        release tarball's generated configure files plus versioned patches.
rec_command:            delete build_requirements() that only adds automake/msys2 for MSVC
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-scope-reduction

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      split-tool-adaptation
fallback_description:   If autoreconf is truly required, adapt automake/autoconf/msys2-equivalent tooling in separate packages or use the
                        repository's approved bootstrap path. Do not hide it inside the CoinUtils package PR.
fallback_command:       create separate tool package adaptation before enabling autoreconf
fallback_auto_fix:      false

forbid_1_pattern:       tool_requires\\(\"automake/.*\"\\).*tool_requires\\(\"msys2/.*\"\\)
forbid_1_reason:        Those tools are unrelated to the OHOS generated-configure build path for CoinUtils 2.11.12.
forbid_1_consequence:   L0 can fail with registry_unreachable before package build evidence is produced.

forbid_2_pattern:       autoreconf.*inside.*coinutils
forbid_2_reason:        Regenerating autotools files changes the dependency and patch surface.
forbid_2_consequence:   The PR mixes toolchain adaptation with the library adaptation.

doc_file:               archives/c/coinutils/2.11.12/knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-coinutils-ohos-tool-requirements-leak.md
last_updated:           2026-09-08
source_event:           coinutils/2.11.12 HarmonyOS PC shadow CI adaptation
source_package:         archives/c/coinutils/2.11.12
evidence:               first shadow run registry_unreachable for automake/msys2, final shadow CI run manual-coinutils-2.11.12-min-20260908T025816Z-22719
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     1
metrics_confidence:     0.82
draft:                  true
